{"sequence": 56, "timestamp": "2026-08-31T09:23:35", "event_type": "response", "payload": {"turn_id": "fcdf0cd1-c489-4032-9a1b-78769e938b14", "response": "In mathematics, several key equations stand out due to their profound impact on various branches:\n\nThe Pythagorean theorem states that in a right triangle, the square of the length of the hypotenuse ($c$) is equal to the sum of the squares of the lengths of the other two sides ($a$ and $b$): \n\n\\[ c^2 = a^2 + b^2 \\]\n\nAnother fundamental concept is Euler’s identity which elegantly links five basic arithmetic operations along with three essential constants from number theory via this simple expression:\n\n\\[\ne^{i\\pi} + 1 = 0 \n\\]", "outcome": "fast_path"}}
